# Test: offline `show config source`/`dump | implied` queries external declarations without starting the run loop, refuses unqueryable binaries, and `ze config show` keeps stdout pure with stderr notice.
# QUESTION: with NO daemon running, when a config names an external endpoint whose
# `run` binary supports `sdk.RunOrDeclare` query mode, do `show config source file <f> | implied | json`
# and `show config dump <f> | implied | json` report the external endpoint's declared
# sends/receives in `implied.participants` without ever starting its run loop; when a
# second config names a nonexistent `run` binary, do both commands refuse non-zero
# naming the endpoint, `run` line, cause, and `ze show plugin conformance run "..."`
# with zero partial implied output; and does `ze config show <f>` write pure written
# config to stdout with the implied notice on stderr? A unit test cannot decide this
# because it proves end-to-end local CLI process execution, real subprocess query-mode
# handshaking, and stdout/stderr separation across all three offline commands.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-explicit-plugin-and-attach-config AC-24, AC-23 (offline notice).
# PREVENTS: offline `| implied` starting external run loops, returning partial implied
# output when a query fails, or polluting `ze config show` stdout with notices.

option=timeout:value=60s

tmpfs=probe.conf:terminator=EOF_PROBE
bus {
	endpoint probe {
		external {
			run "le test fixture plugin/bus-implied-probe probe.started";
		}
		encoding json;
	}
}
bgp {
	filter {
		import { final accept; }
		export { final accept; }
	}
	router-id 192.0.2.254;
	session {
		asn { local 65000; }
	}
	peer edge1 {
		connection {
			remote { ip 192.0.2.1; }
			local { ip auto; }
		}
		session {
			asn { remote 65001; }
		}
	}
}
EOF_PROBE

tmpfs=missing.conf:terminator=EOF_MISSING
bus {
	endpoint broken {
		external {
			run "/nonexistent/ze-missing-implied-probe";
		}
		encoding json;
	}
}
bgp {
	filter {
		import { final accept; }
		export { final accept; }
	}
	router-id 192.0.2.254;
	session {
		asn { local 65000; }
	}
	peer edge1 {
		connection {
			remote { ip 192.0.2.1; }
			local { ip auto; }
		}
		session {
			asn { remote 65001; }
		}
	}
}
EOF_MISSING

# Case 1: query-mode external endpoint appears in implied.participants; run loop never starts.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/bus-assert-implied offline-ok probe.conf probe.started:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: offline-ok verified source and dump implied declarations without starting run loop

# Case 2: nonexistent run binary is refused cleanly with conformance command and zero partial output.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=le test fixture plugin/bus-assert-implied offline-refusal missing.conf broken /nonexistent/ze-missing-implied-probe:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: offline-refusal verified source and dump refuse unqueryable endpoint cleanly

# Case 3: ze config show keeps stdout pure written config and prints implied notice to stderr.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=le test fixture plugin/bus-assert-implied config-show-notice probe.conf:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: config-show-notice verified pure stdout and stderr implied notice
